lines.push("","For any rejected item, the manager must restore only that item and its explicit concept/timing/service binding, preserve all passed companions and shared presentations, and check result/sequence consistency. Do not revert a whole captured case, delete newer historical definitions/timings, transfer FSRS history or copy an original approval onto a changed presentation. The original fallback is a reference, not a claim that the hybrid current presentation has that approval. Dropping only the r7 projection returns the round-six draft, not this original fallback. Use an explicit original-version projection, restoring the original concept and restoring or clearing Current update/Exhibit when the original has none; retain newer archived definitions/timings.","","## Preceding-feedback audit","","All eight reviewer sequence flags were checked in actual runtime order. B19 now tests a distinct MRI acquisition issue: no target/tract, rectus/adductor, core/open or favored-corridor instruction remains in its earlier task or feedback. Its old P/Q/R table is removed; A/B first appear in the unchanged completed MRI report. Other revised precursors avoid teaching the later passed answer; B18's prior discussion eligibility remains visible topic overlap, while the later abnormal-node/nonrepresentative-aspirate finding still determines the actual staging procedure.","","Two recorded caveats cannot be repaired within the freeze. B21-context is PASS and still contains its existing authoring phrase about the passed management premise. B22-context is PASS and still partly discourages the later repeat-endoscopy distractor. Neither is among the eleven authorized revisions. They remain exact, with the reviewer limitation carried forward; no fresh independent sequence difficulty is claimed. See the eight-row audit in the response ledger and its machine-readable artifact.","","## Validation","","| Check | Exact normal result |","| --- | --- |");
